</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>OP-GRPO Training Setup</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the VerL framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheng et al., 2024</a>]</cite> to apply the GRPO training pipeline. We map each rate to a capped ladder-style
reward so that improvements in coverage and diversity translate into discrete,
interpretable gains during optimization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The maximum scaled rewards are capped at
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{cov}}=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{cov}}=1.5</annotation></semantics></math> for coverage and <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{uniq}}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{uniq}}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> for uniqueness.
For the coverage rate <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{cov}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the scaled reward is assigned as</p>
<table id="A5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{cov}}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }r_{\mathrm{cov}}=0,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }0&lt;r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.2,\\
0.6&amp;\text{if }0.2\leq r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.4,\\
0.9&amp;\text{if }0.4\leq r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.6,\\
1.2&amp;\text{if }0.6\leq r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.8,\\
1.5&amp;\text{if }r_{\mathrm{cov}}\geq 0.8,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.6</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.9</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1.2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1.5</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{cov}}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }r_{\mathrm{cov}}=0,\\
0.3&amp;\text{if }0&lt;r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.2,\\
0.6&amp;\text{if }0.2\leq r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.4,\\
0.9&amp;\text{if }0.4\leq r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.6,\\
1.2&amp;\text{if }0.6\leq r_{\mathrm{cov}}&lt;0.8,\\
1.5&amp;\text{if }r_{\mathrm{cov}}\geq 0.8,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">while the uniqueness rate <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{uniq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{uniq}}</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to</p>
<table id="A5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{uniq}}=\begin{cases}0.3&amp;\text{if }r_{\mathrm{uniq}}=1.0,\\
0.2&amp;\text{if }0.8&lt;r_{\mathrm{uniq}}&lt;1.0,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }0.6&lt;r_{\mathrm{uniq}}\leq 0.8,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.3</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{uniq}}=\begin{cases}0.3&amp;\text{if }r_{\mathrm{uniq}}=1.0,\\
0.2&amp;\text{if }0.8&lt;r_{\mathrm{uniq}}&lt;1.0,\\
0.1&amp;\text{if }0.6&lt;r_{\mathrm{uniq}}\leq 0.8,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These scaled values replace the linear terms
<math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{cov}}r_{\mathrm{cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{cov}}r_{\mathrm{cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{uniq}}r_{\mathrm{uniq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>uniq</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{uniq}}r_{\mathrm{uniq}}</annotation></semantics></math>
in Eq. <a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 4.3 Construction of Reward Functions ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Overton Pluralistic Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, yielding the final scalar reward used during GRPO training.
This ladder-style shaping encourages incremental improvements: partial coverage or moderate
uniqueness still receives positive reinforcement, while higher-quality outputs obtain
clearly larger rewards. Compared to continuous linear scaling, the stepwise mapping stabilizes
optimization by providing discrete reward levels and reducing sensitivity to minor similarity
fluctuations, thereby guiding training toward meaningful qualitative improvements rather than
overfitting to fine-grained score variations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Robustness to NLI backbone and calibration</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluation in Overton Pluralism relies on NLI-based scoring and LLM-as-judge components, whose configurations (e.g., backbone choice and decision thresholds) may influence absolute metric values. To ensure a fair and controlled comparison, all methods are evaluated using the same backbone model, identical thresholds, and the official Modular Pluralism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng et al. [2024]</a></cite> evaluation pipeline. This setup prevents confounding factors arising from evaluator differences and allows a direct comparison of modeling approaches.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To further examine robustness, we repeat the full NLI evaluation using two additional NLI backbones,
<span id="A5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">roberta-large-snli_mnli_fever_anli_R1_R2_R3-nli</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al. [2020]</a></cite>
and <span id="A5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">xlm-roberta-large-xnli</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Conneau et al. [2020]</a></cite>, and also increase the minimum accuracy threshold from <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.
As shown in Tables <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ E.3 Robustness to NLI backbone and calibration ‣ Appendix E Additional Evaluation Details ‣ Overton Pluralistic Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and <a href="#A5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ E.3 Robustness to NLI backbone and calibration ‣ Appendix E Additional Evaluation Details ‣ Overton Pluralistic Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, across all evaluation configurations, <span id="A5.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implicit OP-GRPO</span> consistently outperforms Explicit OP Prompting and Modular Pluralism on both coverage and accuracy metrics. The performance gap remains substantial under all NLI backbones, demonstrating that the advantages of Implicit OP-GRPO are stable across evaluator choices and are not tied to a specific calibration setting. These results confirm that the improvements stem from the training objective itself rather than from evaluation artifacts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T8" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T8.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T8.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5 p (Avg./Acc@0.5)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T8.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10 p (Avg./Acc@0.5)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="A5.T8.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Explicit OP Prompting</td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">23.2 / 10.1</td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">14.4 / 2.7</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T8.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T8.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A5.T8.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implicit OP-GRPO (ours)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.T8.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">41.3 / 31.1</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.T8.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">24.0 / 8.9</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T8.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T8.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" rowspan="2"><span id="A5.T8.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Explicit OP Prompting</td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">24.4 / 10.5</td>
<td id="A5.T8.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">17.2 / 4.3</td></tr>
